# Market data (RSI/MACD/backtests/everything) no longer needs a browser-side
# key at all — it's synced once a day by a GitHub Action into
# public/market-data.json, which the app fetches at runtime. To enable that
# sync, set TWELVE_DATA_KEY as a repo secret (Settings > Secrets and
# variables > Actions), NOT here — this file is only for browser-side
# (VITE_-prefixed) variables. Get a free key at https://twelvedata.com.

# Optional. Without this, the price shown updates only once a day (from the
# synced snapshot above). With it, US stock/ETF prices update every ~30s via
# a lightweight client-side polling loop — a display-only overlay, doesn't
# affect any indicator or backtest.
# Get a free key at https://finnhub.io (free tier: 60 requests/min)
VITE_FINNHUB_KEY=

# Optional. Without these, "Simulate a trade", "My trades" and the feedback
# form each show a not-configured message instead of breaking. Powers the hypothetical
# paper-trading feature: silent anonymous accounts (no email, no password,
# no visible sign-in step — see AuthContext.ensureSession) and storage for
# user-created simulated positions, and the feedback form (same anonymous
# identity, its own table). The user always picks their own direction/size —
# the app only tracks outcomes, never recommends.
# Free project at https://supabase.com. After creating one: (1) run
# supabase/schema.sql in the project's SQL editor (re-run it after pulling
# changes — it is idempotent, and the feedback table was added later), (2) enable
# Authentication > Sign In / Providers > Anonymous Sign-Ins (off by
# default), (3) copy these two values from Project Settings > API. The
# anon/publishable key is meant to be public — Supabase's security model is
# row-level security in Postgres, not secrecy of this key.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
